<!-- The look every level shares: a filmic curve so the emissive bricks do not clip flat, a haze
     at the far end of the field, and enough bloom to make them read as neon rather than plastic.

     Each child is one thing that decides how the frame looks, and it is on because the element
     is here — there is no value that means "off". Tuning the game's look is this one file.

     `threshold` is the one to understand: it is how bright a pixel has to be before it glows,
     where 1 is white. At 1 only what is brighter than white blooms, which in this scene was the
     ball and nothing else. At 0.5 the emissive paddle and the lit brick faces come in too. -->
<Render>
  <Fog color="#05070d" near="20" far="46" />
  <ToneMapping curve="ACESFilmicToneMapping" exposure="1.05" />
  <Bloom strength="0.5" radius="0.45" threshold="0.5" />
</Render>
